Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Data and mathematical definitions", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"af0f84c5-5af2-4436-9f1b-a43de77b03aa"],

Cell["Machine learning modular forms | 1 of 4", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"b27bd187-3fcf-4142-a89e-18355530f476"],

Cell["\<\
Exact Fourier coefficients for eta powers, CHL eta products and \
Eisenstein-series examples. Evaluate the setup first, then read and evaluate \
the sections you need. The small examples are inexpensive, and dataset \
exports are opt-in. Coefficient positions and target definitions are retained \
with the data.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9994934295399227`*^9, 
  3.999493431314623*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"23f48452-04bb-4ba3-9477-\
a7798fca8fba"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1412e4ee-47a0-4c3d-bf8e-77b3e0acaa2e"],

Cell["\<\
Keep the notebooks, support and example_results directories together. Each \
notebook can be opened in a fresh kernel. Definitions in this notebook are \
local to its notebook context; the shared packages provide the same data and \
training routines used by the additional-validation study.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b1576916-9a89-4b09-ba4e-9bcdb85364ae"],

